Title: 0018-aros-close-sdl-at-exit
Repository: pragtical
Base-Commit: 5c05f09e081833b581fb5ecd10e64963dec87f03
Requires: 0017-coalesce-window-size-events.patch
Author: aros-pragtical project
Date: 2026-11-18
Upstream-Status: local-only
Scope: AROS only, src/main.c.

Problem:
  An exit() from an error path (for example a failed window surface) skips SDL_AppQuit and SDL_Quit. AROS does not close a program's windows when it ends, so the editor window stayed on the screen with no program behind it.
Solution:
  Register SDL_Quit as an exit handler after SDL_Init on AROS. A second SDL_Quit after the normal shutdown does nothing.
Validation:
  2026-11-18, AROS One 1.3 and mainline nightly 20261113 under QEMU: after the forced exit the window is closed; without the patch it stayed on the screen.
Removal:
  Permanent for the AROS port.

diff --git a/src/main.c b/src/main.c
index dff13090..e2786cc4 100644
--- a/src/main.c
+++ b/src/main.c
@@ -353,6 +353,12 @@ SDL_AppResult SDL_AppInit(void **appstate, int argc, char *argv[]) {
     return SDL_APP_FAILURE;
   }
   SDL_SetEventEnabled(SDL_EVENT_DROP_FILE, true);
+#ifdef __AROS__
+  /* An exit() from an error path skips SDL_AppQuit and the SDL_Quit after it.
+   * AROS does not close a program's windows for it, so the window would stay
+   * on the screen with nothing behind it. */
+  atexit(SDL_Quit);
+#endif
 
   if (ren_init() != 0) {
     fprintf(stderr, "Error initializing renderer: %s\n", SDL_GetError());
